# MEDIA STAYS OUT OF GIT — it syncs via Google Drive, not the repo.
# GitHub hard-limits files at 100MB and the refs library alone is 186MB.
# The repo carries CODE + PLANS + DOCS + LEDGERS: everything needed to
# rebuild any video once the media lands beside it.

assets/refs/
assets/bgm/
assets/nev/wardrobe/
assets/nev/accessories/
assets/nev/_contact/
projects/*/clips/
projects/*/output/
projects/*/tmp/
projects/*/audio/*.wav
projects/_archive/
*.mp4
*.wav
*.zip

__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store

# KEPT IN GIT on purpose (small, and they ARE the project):
#   assets/nev/face/          the 6-image identity set (~700KB) - generations need it
#   assets/nev/index.json     the measured metadata
#   assets/pillars/           the measured profiles - every gate reads these
#   projects/*/audio/*.json   declared cut lists (actual post-blend boundaries)
#   projects/*/analysis/*.png storyboards + evidence strips
#   ledgers/                  rejects + lessons - MERGE on conflict, never overwrite
